{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Parallelism 2 but tests not actually split",
    "Explanation": [
      "The config sets `parallelism: 2`, and the log confirms two containers ran (CIRCLE_NODE_TOTAL=2, indices 0 and 1). `circleci tests split` did compute a correct per-node partition (node 0 got test_goodbye.sh, node 1 got test_hello.sh), so the split list itself was divided. However, the run loop iterates over `src/test_*.sh` (the raw glob) instead of the contents of /tmp/split.txt, so every node ran the full suite (both tests). The self-check then failed on both nodes (`Ran 2 file(s); split list had 1`), producing a red build. The suite therefore did not actually split across nodes; the work was duplicated. The fix is to actually consume the output of `circleci tests split` (e.g., loop over `$(cat /tmp/split.txt)` or pipe the glob into split and xargs), without changing the workflow structure or parallelism level."
