{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Deploy Job Needs Beta Tag Filters",
    "Explanation": [
      "The workflow output shows pipeline #156 completed with every job SUCCESS, so the pipeline is green. However, the trigger was a plain branch commit (branch koans-09-tag-filters, commit de37612, no tag), and the deploy job still ran. The requirement states deploy must only run for tags matching the beta product (e.g. beta-main-0.1.1) and never for alpha- tags or untagged branch commits, so the observed behaviour is incorrect. The config has no `filters` on the deploy job in the workflow; `requires` only controls ordering, not when a job is eligible to run. The fix is to add a filters block to the `deploy` job in the workflow: `filters: { tags: { only: /^beta-.*/ }, branches: { ignore: /.*/ } }`. Because CircleCI does not run jobs on tag pipelines unless they have tag filters, the upstream `build` and `test` jobs that deploy requires must also be given `filters: tags: only: /.*/` so they execute on the beta tag and allow deploy to run; the beta-only restriction itself belongs on the deploy job."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
      "  \"fix\": \"filters_tags_only_beta\",",
      "  \"fix_target_job\": \"deploy\",",
      "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
